BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Oct 22 | An Evening with Amna Nawaz of the PBS News Hour
DTSTART:20261022T190000
DTEND:20261022T203000
DTSTAMP:20261021T155930Z
UID:4af300eb140279eb0299902e263cda@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:An evening with Amna Nawaz\, co-anchor & co-managing editor of
  the PBS News Hour Go behind the headlines with one of the most trusted vo
 ices in American journalism. Join Vermont Public for an evening with Amna 
 Nawaz \, co‑anchor of PBS News Hour\, for an intimate\, wide‑ranging c
 onversation hosted by Vermont Public’s Mitch Wertlieb . For the past eig
 ht years\, Amna has helped lead one of the country’s longest‑running n
 ightly news broadcasts—on the air since 1975—bringing clarity\, contex
 t\, and humanity to the stories shaping our world. As the midterm election
 s approach\, Amna will share what PBS News is focusing on right now\, and 
 why it matters. Hear firsthand how national and international stories are 
 reported— from anchoring News Hour at the U.S. Southern border to Israel
  in the aftermath of the October 7 attacks\, to Kyiv\, Ukraine\, following
  her interview with President Volodymyr Zelenskyy. She’ll also pull back
  the curtain on how PBS NewsHour is evolving amid changes to CPB funding. 
 This is a rare opportunity to step inside the newsroom\, understand how th
 e news gets made\, and engage with the journalism that helps inform our de
 mocracy. Click or tap here to purchase tickets. PLEASE NOTE: Tickets are O
 NLY sold via lebanonoperahouse.org \, in person at the Box Office at Leban
 on Opera House\, or by phone at 603.448.0400. Tickets: General admission: 
 $28 Students and seniors: $18 Generous admission: $48 Schedule Doors open:
  6 p.m Event begins: 7 p.m Event ends: 8:30 p.m. This event is made possib
 le with support from Primmer Piper Eggleston and Cramer . Accommodations V
 ermont Public is committed to providing access and accommodation for indiv
 iduals with disabilities at our events. To request accommodations\, please
  email events@vermontpublic.org or call us at 802-655-9451 at least seven 
 days in advance of the event. Cancellation Policy From the Lebanon Opera H
 ouse: all ticket sales are final and non-refundable Directions and Parking
  Lebanon Opera House is located at 51 North Park Street\, Lebanon\, New Ha
 mpshire 03766 . Free parking is available along Colburn Park (Lebanon Gree
 n) and surrounding streets. Public parking can be found in the lot directl
 y behind Lebanon Opera House via Flynn Street and Court Street. Other ques
 tions? Email us at events@vermontpublic.org .\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Lebanon Opera House\, 51 North Park St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/oct-22-an-
 evening-with-amna-nawaz-of-the-pbs-news-hour-01-09-2026-09-44-34
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paul Winter: This Glorious Earth
DTSTART:20261022T190000
DTEND:20261022T203000
DTSTAMP:20261021T155930Z
UID:cb96e54900c3bb7f17f0a5b5dc742a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Grammy Award-winning composer and saxophonist Paul Winter brin
 gs This Glorious Earth to Chandler. Joined by pianist Henrique Eisenmann\,
  Winter will blend soprano saxophone and piano with the voices of whales\,
  wolves\, wood thrushes\, and other members of what he calls “the greate
 r symphony of the Earth.” Eisenmann brings a background in Brazilian mus
 ic\, European classical traditions\, and jazz to their musical partnership
 . He has spent the past five years touring internationally with the Paul W
 inter Consort and performing in a duo with Winter. The concert is presente
 d alongside Marjorie Ryerson’s Water Music exhibition in Chandler Galler
 y\, connecting music\, the natural world\, and a shared commitment to cele
 brating and preserving Earth and its beauty. Winter wrote the introduction
  to Ryerson’s book\, describing her work as something that “opens our 
 eyes again to water’s miraculous beauty and life-giving power.”\n\nSou
 rces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Chandler Center for the Arts\, 71 N. Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/paul-winte
 r-this-glorious-earth-09-10-2026-19-16-31
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Webinar: Boosting Rural Downtown Development
DTSTART:20261022T120000
DTEND:20261022T133000
DTSTAMP:20261021T155930Z
UID:be8d17834b8a8926888755237b0317@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Northern Forest Center for the next webinar in its Bu
 ilding the New Forest Future series\, Boosting Rural Downtown Development
 \, at noon on Thursday\, Oct. 22. You’ll hear from three organizations s
 upporting downtown business development in the Northern Forest\, which str
 etches across New York\, Vermont\, New Hampshire\, and Maine. They’ll di
 scuss different models for business support and share examples of how thei
 r work has helped businesses and communities grow. The panel will be facil
 itated by Maura Adams\, director of community investment at the Northern F
 orest Center. Panelists include: • Kristina Cannon\, President & CEO of 
 Main Street Skowhegan • Wendy Fahlbeck\, Executive Director of Coös Eco
 nomic Development Corporation • Loralee Tester\, Director of the Northea
 st Kingdom Chamber of Commerce The Center’s Building the New Forest Futu
 re webinar series amplifies stories\, practices\, and lessons from rural c
 ommunity and economic development in the Northern Forest — which spans a
 cross New York\, Vermont\, New Hampshire\, and Maine. Intended for communi
 ty leaders\, funders\, and policymakers\, it provides inspiration and prac
 tical guidance for fostering thriving rural forest-based communities. Regi
 stration is free but required. Zoom\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/webinar-bo
 osting-rural-downtown-development-09-10-2026-09-57-44
END:VEVENT
